# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZYLO Express — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Values here are placeholders only.
#
# Deliberately no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefixes: that prefix inlines a value into the
# browser bundle. Every Supabase call in this app is made server-side, so no
# key needs to reach the client.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Supabase -------------------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API
SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-ref
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Publishable ("anon") key — subject to Row Level Security.
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Secret key — BYPASSES Row Level Security. Server-only. Rotate if leaked.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Legacy service-role JWT. Needed by the seed script and Edge Function deploys.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# --- Cache (Upstash Redis, REST transport) --------------------------------
# Optional. Blank => in-memory LRU fallback, which is per-instance and resets
# on deploy. Fine for local dev; set these in production.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# --- Site -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute origin, no trailing slash. Drives canonical URLs, OG tags, sitemap,
# and the OAuth return address.
#
# Set this per environment. It builds the `redirect_to` handed to Supabase when
# a customer signs in with Google, and Supabase checks that value against the
# Redirect URLs allow-list in its dashboard. A stale value here is the usual
# cause of a Google sign-in that returns to the wrong host or is refused
# outright. See supabase/README.md §5.
#
# On Vercel this may be omitted: `src/lib/site-url.ts` falls back to
# VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL, then VERCEL_URL, both injected by the platform.
# That fallback is correct for metadata but NOT for OAuth on preview
# deployments, whose per-deployment hostname can never be in Supabase's
# allow-list. Set it explicitly in production regardless — inference is a
# convenience, not a configuration strategy. See VERCEL.md.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Paystack (cards + M-Pesa) --------------------------------------------
# Dashboard → Settings → API Keys & Webhooks.
#
# These are now a FALLBACK. Paystack is configured from the portal — Settings →
# Paystack — which stores the keys in `payment_credentials`, a table only the
# server can read, and lets an operator switch between sandbox and production
# without a deploy. Whatever is saved there wins; these are used when nothing
# has been.
#
# Keeping them means an existing deployment upgrades with nothing to do, and a
# fresh clone still runs before anybody has opened the portal.
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional. Paystack's public key authorises their browser-side Inline popup;
# this app initialises transactions on the server and redirects to Paystack's
# hosted page instead, so no card number ever touches this origin. Stored for
# completeness — nothing reads it today.
# PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# The currency your Paystack account settles in. M-Pesa is only offered on
# Kenyan accounts, so KES is the default; NGN, GHS, ZAR and USD also exist
# depending on where the account is registered.
PAYSTACK_CURRENCY=KES

# Webhook: point Paystack at https://<your-domain>/api/payments/paystack/webhook
# The handler authenticates deliveries with an HMAC-SHA512 of the raw body
# keyed by the secret key above — no extra shared secret to configure.

# --- PayPal ----------------------------------------------------------------
# developer.paypal.com → Apps & Credentials. Sandbox and live are separate
# credential pairs; switching environments means swapping both, not just the
# flag below.
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# `live` selects api-m.paypal.com. Anything else (including blank) stays on
# api-m.sandbox.paypal.com, so a missing value can never charge a real card.
PAYPAL_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# Webhook id from the dashboard, for https://<your-domain>/api/payments/paypal/webhook
# PayPal signs webhooks against this id and verifies them via their own API.
# Leave blank and the webhook route rejects every delivery rather than trusting
# an unverifiable one — the redirect capture still completes orders.
PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=

# --- Payment FX -----------------------------------------------------------
# The catalogue is priced in USD; Paystack Kenya can only charge KES. These are
# the rates used to convert an order total into the amount the provider is
# asked to move. Both the USD total and the converted amount are recorded on
# every payment row, so books reconcile even after a rate changes.
#
# These are static fallbacks, not a pricing strategy. A real deployment should
# feed them from an FX provider on a schedule and widen the spread to cover
# settlement risk. Blank uses the built-in defaults in src/lib/payments/currency.ts.
FX_USD_KES=
FX_USD_NGN=
FX_USD_GHS=
FX_USD_ZAR=

# --- Sign in with Google --------------------------------------------------
# No variables needed here. The Google client ID and secret are configured in
# the Supabase dashboard (Authentication → Providers → Google), never in this
# file — the browser and this app only ever talk to Supabase, not to Google.
